# The NOX onion service. Written by the NOX install script and written again
# on every run of it: change the server's port with the script, not here.
#
# Where tor keeps the onion service's key. tor writes the onion address to the
# file "hostname" in it. Keep this directory: without it the address changes.
HiddenServiceDir "@HS_DIR@"
# Port 443 of the onion address leads to the NOX server on this machine, over
# loopback: tor's connections reach the server from there, and the server
# listens on every address (0.0.0.0), loopback among them.
HiddenServicePort 443 127.0.0.1:@PORT@
# Proof of work against floods of requests: under load, tor serves first the
# clients that solved a small puzzle. The NOX app solves them on its own.
HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
# Proof of work limits new circuits, not the streams on one already open, and
# the address is open to anyone who knows it. A device needs one stream for
# its socket and a few for file transfers; a circuit that opens more than 16
# at once is closed, so a stranger cannot pile silent streams onto one paid
# circuit.
HiddenServiceMaxStreams 16
HiddenServiceMaxStreamsCloseCircuit 1
